They are similar in overall philosophy, but they are optimized for **different purposes**.  
Your current prompt is a **production worksheet generator**: give it the three Stage 1 files and get back a one-page student-facing PDF.  
The Hitaansh prompt is closer to a **full curriculum-generation and auditing system**: it derives an internal playbook, checks source alignment, handles missing concepts, generates instructor metadata, maintains attribution, and supports multiple output formats in addition to generating the case itself.  
